{
  "root_node": "source.raw.customer",
  "cause": "upstream_data",
  "action": "escalate",
  "evidence": "The stg_customers model failed contract validation because its column account_balance is defined as VARCHAR, while the staging contract expects DECIMAL(15,2). The raw source column c_acctbal is VARCHAR. Profiling shows conversion to DECIMAL(15,2) is not lossless: raw values have at most 1 decimal place, so converting to 2 decimal places would add missing digits that cannot be recovered. According to team policy, type changes can only be patched if lossless; here they are not, so the issue must be escalated to the source owner. The problem originates at raw.customer."
}
